## Sportarr stores its data in an SQLite database inside /config by default.
## No database setup is required.
##
## To use PostgreSQL instead, set Sportarr__Database__Provider to 'postgres'
## and fill in the connection settings below. Any other value (including
## blank) uses SQLite, and the remaining settings are ignored.
##
## PostgreSQL is supported for fresh installs only. There is no migration
## path from an existing SQLite database.

# Database settings
Sportarr__Database__Host=''
Sportarr__Database__Name='sportarr<__instance>'
Sportarr__Database__Password=''
Sportarr__Database__Port='5432'
Sportarr__Database__Provider=''
Sportarr__Database__Username='sportarr<__instance>'
